   "gap": "Grinstead-Snell CHANCE version of 4 July 2006, sec. 1.2, p. 26 (PDF p. 34), immediately after Definition 1.3, states that there is no single correct choice of sample space for an experiment (two coin tosses recorded as {HH,HT,TH,TT} or as {0,1,2}), contrasts the induced distribution (1/4, 1/2, 1/4) on {0,1,2} with the uniform distribution (1/3, 1/3, 1/3) there, and makes the empirical claim that the latter, though a valid distribution function, is not consistent with observed data on coin tossing. The handbook definition and remark (finite-probability.tex lines 24-55) say only that uniform weights are an assumption; neither the modelling claim about the choice of sample space nor the empirical claim (the source states no design or uncertainty for it) is supplied anywhere on the route.",
