   "gap": "Grinstead-Snell CHANCE version of 4 July 2006, Definition 4.2 (p. 141, PDF p. 149) gives the equivalent complemented form of mutual independence (for every choice of each event or its complement, the probability of the full intersection is the product). The route proves only that complementing preserves independence (independent-random-variables.tex thm:p15-independence-basic item 2); the converse, that these full-product identities for all complement choices imply mutual independence, is not stated or proved. The same page states that the single identity P(A_1 and ... and A_n) = P(A_1)...P(A_n) does not imply mutual independence; the route only remarks that checking the full intersection is not this definition (independent-random-variables.tex lines 37-38) and gives no counterexample or argument. Definition 4.4 for n random variables is supplied on the route in independent-random-variables.tex.",
