   "gap": "The source counterparts of this worked base-rate example are Grinstead-Snell CHANCE version of 4 July 2006 Examples 4.16 and 4.17 (pp. 146-147, PDF pp. 154-155). Example 4.16 estimates priors and test-outcome probabilities from national records of 10,000 people having one of three diseases and two tests (Tables 4.3 and 4.4); Example 4.17 uses prior .001, P(+|cancer) = .99 and P(-|no cancer) = .95, obtains posterior .019 with 98.1 percent of positives false, and reports that over half of a group of second-year medical students guessed a posterior above .5. The handbook substitutes stipulated hypothetical weights (finite-probability.tex lines 280-343) and supplies none of these empirical claims with their task, population, design and uncertainty.",
