   "gap": "The source counterpart of this indicator-counting example is Grinstead-Snell CHANCE version of 4 July 2006 Example 6.8 (p. 232, PDF p. 240): the number F of fixed points of a uniformly random permutation of {1, ..., n} is a sum of n dependent indicators each with mean 1/n, so E(F) = 1 for every n (with the table check E(Y) = 1 for n = 3). The handbook example (finite-probability.tex lines 386-399) illustrates the principle with one event counted twice and does not supply this source result or its random-permutation model anywhere on the route.",
